# TT.OSAG_NOTIFY -- event_notify and is_notify_suppressor_active. The registered-listener
# cursors (S-NOTIFY-012..014) join auth.permission / auth.mv_service_access, materialized
# views on both engines that are empty in both containers and cannot be fed by a rolled-back
# fixture (Oracle's MV refresh commits), so the dispatch path exercised here is the
# connectivity-event local-contact path (S-NOTIFY-010, S-NOTIFY-029): group-1 event type
# 10001 on a host whose address has on-site intervention contacts with an SMS or an email
# notification. Also covered: the suppression gate (S-NOTIFY-006/023: active window with
# disable_notification = 1 suppresses, a question event 50008 passes anyway, an active window
# without the flag and an expired window do not suppress), the automatic-event cap early exit
# (S-NOTIFY-004), the customer notify-count bump reaching 5 with its 20010 limit event
# (S-NOTIFY-015), notify_local_contacts' NO_DATA_FOUND arm when the ticket has no service
# (S-NOTIFY-029: nothing sent, counter untouched), and the swallow-all contract for a
# nonexistent event / ticket (S-NOTIFY-001/002/007: no error reaches the caller).
#
# SEND PATHS (observed live 2026-10-21, Oracle 23.7 container): OSAG.OSAG_MSG.send_mail opens
# UTL_SMTP to localhost:25 and fails with ORA-24247 (network access denied by ACL) -- it logs
# and RE-RAISES (ddl/src/pkgb/osag_osag_msg.sql:60-70); send_sms delegates to send_mail and
# SWALLOWS (lines 91-94). Hence on Oracle an SMS local-contact notification "succeeds" (the
# 20003 event is written, the counter bumps) while an email one aborts event_notify through
# its outer WHEN OTHERS (S-NOTIFY-001) before the 20001 event and the counter update. The
# PostgreSQL translation queues both into osag.msg_outbox (S-MSG-013) and continues. The
# email path (ticket 958121) is therefore the documented difference in known.diff.
#
# ORA_USER=system: the fixtures insert into stop.company, stop.contact, mss.address, mss.host,
# mss.service, mss.local_contact(_notification); TT holds only SELECT on those. Rolled back.
ORA_USER=system
COMMITS=no
COMPARE_MSG=no
DESCRIPTION=event_notify local-contact SMS/email paths, suppression gate, cap early exit, 20010 limit event, swallow-all; is_notify_suppressor_active true/false on tickets 958120-958125
